Using final answer URLs for evaluation: ['I can do that — but I need one quick clarification: can you confirm exactly which connector your monitor has (or send a photo)?\n\nHow to identify it (quick checks):\n- DVI (looks most like HDMI but larger): wide rectangular with a flat blade on one side plus a grid of pins. DVI-D has only digital pins; DVI-I includes extra analog pins around the flat blade.\n- DisplayPort (DP): rectangular with one side slightly angled and often a latch button on the cable end.\n- Mini DisplayPort / Thunderbolt: small rectangular (about as wide as a USB-A is tall).\n- VGA: trapezoid D?sub with 15 round pins and two screw posts.\n\nImportant compatibility notes:\n- If the monitor is DVI (digital/DVI-D), a simple HDMI-to-DVI cable or passive adapter will usually work (video only; DVI typically doesn’t carry audio).\n- If the monitor is VGA (analog), you’ll need an active HDMI?VGA converter (HDMI is digital; VGA is analog). These usually require power (USB) and are a little bulkier.\n- If the monitor is DisplayPort (full-size) or MiniDP, converting from HDMI source to DP monitor requires an active HDMI?DP converter (more expensive and less common). Passive cables won’t work.\n- If it’s DVI-I, HDMI can still feed the digital pins, but analog pins won’t be used.\n- Make sure which direction you need: HDMI source ? monitor input. Some adapters only work the other way (DP source ? HDMI monitor).\n\nIf you can tell me which connector it is (or upload a photo), I’ll search all four shops and return all matching offers (I’ll note any active vs passive requirement and list exact product links).']
